    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Pounding noises kept coming from the bathroom in a suburban home outside Portland, Oregon. Police officers had arrived. All of them were holding guns. After shouting that they were police, they ordered the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "burglar",
            "zh": "入室窃贼"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to let them in."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "No response. Just more pounding noises. Perhaps, the police thought, the burglar was trying to open a window and run away."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "All at once, the police officers broke in, ready to fire."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Then, they saw it: a little robot vacuum cleaner. The robot was stuck in a corner. It was knocking repeatedly into the shower door. The bathroom floor was very clean. “There was just immediate laughter,” Danny DiPietro, one of the police officers, said in an interview."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The call for help was no joke. A man dialed 911 to report that someone had broken into a home. “The burglar was locked in the bathroom,” the caller said. “I could see shadows moving under the door.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The man was "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "house-sitting",
            "zh": "代人照看房子"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for his nephew, who was away on business. He went out to walk the dog. When he came back, he heard something in the bathroom. The man didn’t know his nephew owned a robot vacuum cleaner."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The man was sorry for sending a false alarm. The police, however, told him, “Hey, we believed it was a burglar, too. You were house-sitting. How could you know this vacuum cleaner was going to do this?”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“Every call is important,” DiPietro said. “This is just a fun one. We will remember it for a long time for a good reason!”"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
